|~ `::nullable`, the mark in a shape of a part null in some of the data,
   and the laws declared under it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:nullable
  |~~ A nullable marks, in the shape of a value, a part that is null in
      some of the data and of the shape under the mark in the rest:
      `[1 null 3] | shape` answers `::shape[::nullable::number]`, and a
      record that is null in some is `::nullable` over the record, so the
      paths of the data read on through the mark,
      `[{:author {:login "a"}} {:author null}] | shape | get /0/author/login`
      answering `::string`. A part that is null alone stands as `::null`,
      and kinds that part stand as the set of them under the mark,
      `::nullable#[::number ::string]`; null is never among the kinds of
      that set. `query` reads such a part softly, and a default stands
      for the null, `query /author/login "-"`.
      ::link~(::shape | doc) ::link~(::absent | doc)
      ::link~(::any/query | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :marksAPartNullInSomeOfTheData
        |~~ A part null in some of the data stands marked nullable. ~~|
        ~([1 null 3] | shape | eq ::shape[::nullable::number])
    | proves :readsThePathsOfTheDataThroughIt
        |~~ The paths of the data read on through the mark. ~~|
        ~([{:author {:login "a"}} {:author null}] | shape | get /0/author/login | eq ::string)
    | proves :standsOverTheKindsThatPart
        |~~ Kinds that part stand under the mark, null not among them. ~~|
        ~([1 "a" null] | shape | eq ::shape[::nullable#[::number ::string]])
    | proves :leavesANullAloneAsItsKind
        |~~ A part that is null alone stands as its kind. ~~|
        ~({:next null} | shape | eq ::shape{:next ::null})
